<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  One grown citrus as a trunk and a single ellipsoid: 3.12 m across, 2.76 m to
  the top, with 0.44 m of trunk showing under the crown.

  This is the crown these worlds were first planted with, kept because it is
  still the right answer to a fair number of questions. A row of ellipsoids and
  a row of meshes stand on the same ground, throw the same shadow and stop a
  lidar ray at about the same distance; what they do not do is look alike to a
  camera. So a block planted round is the control: anything a perception stack
  does differently between a round talhao and a mesh one came from the foliage
  and not from the geometry of the field.

  The ellipsoid is the sphere model://citrus_tree's mesh is pushed out of,
  averaged round in plan — which is why the mesh measures 3.95 m across and
  this measures 3.12 m. Lobes stand proud of the sphere they came from; a
  smooth surface has nothing to stand proud with, and pretending otherwise by
  inflating the ellipsoid would make the control the odd one out.

  It has a trunk, and the first cut of this model did not. A crown resting on
  the ground is what these worlds used to draw, and it reads as a shrub or as a
  ball someone left in the field; a citrus of this age carries its skirt about
  half a metre up. That trunk is a second visual and therefore a second entity,
  which doubles what a round talhao costs — the reason to accept it is that a
  tree without a trunk is not a control for anything, it is a different plant.

  Nothing collides. See model://citrus_tree for why that is true of all four
  trees.
-->
<sdf version="1.10">
  <model name="citrus_round">
    <static>true</static>

    <link name="tree">
      <visual name="trunk">
        <pose>0 0 0.45 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry>
          <cylinder>
            <radius>0.13</radius>
            <length>0.9</length>
          </cylinder>
        </geometry>
        <material>
          <ambient>0.12 0.09 0.07 1</ambient>
          <diffuse>0.29 0.23 0.17 1</diffuse>
          <specular>0.05 0.05 0.05 1</specular>
        </material>
      </visual>

      <visual name="canopy">
        <pose>0 0 1.60 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry>
          <ellipsoid><radii>1.56 1.56 1.16</radii></ellipsoid>
        </geometry>
        <material>
          <ambient>0.06 0.13 0.05 1</ambient>
          <diffuse>0.16 0.36 0.12 1</diffuse>
          <specular>0.05 0.05 0.05 1</specular>
        </material>
      </visual>
    </link>

  </model>
</sdf>
